{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513213-discipline-derangements-your-opinion","id":1513213,"title":"Discipline derangements... your opinion?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-29T11:10:39-07:00","id":1513213,"title":"Discipline derangements... your opinion?","content":"Lately there were quite a few thread about disciplines and their effects, and I started to wonder, whats your, my dear fellow Storytellers and players, opinion in the phenomenon called Discipline derangements<br /> Even before Players Guide to High and Low Clans detailed it, the idea lingered above Vampire, but those books went in details.<br /> So the idea is, thanks to the Disciplines a Vampire might have incredible power at her disposal.... but such power can (and often does) also begin to affect her mentally.<br /> Just as some mortal lords become corrupt and degenerate because of the power they wield over their fellow humans, a Cainite might find her sanity eroded by the powers of the &quot;Gifts&quot; of Caine.<br /> When to afflict \u201cDiscipline derangements\u201d is ultimately up to the Storyteller.<br /> In general, only characters who have a Discipline at level 6 or above are in danger of developing Discipline derangements,<b> but if the player and Storyteller agree</b>, such a derangement <i><b>might come at earlier levels.</b></i><br /> Depending of certain factors, these could be either temporary or parmanent Discipline derangements<br /> There are some examples from those books, but of course, Storytellers and Players are encouraged to come up with their own ideas<br /> <br /> <b>Animal Personification </b>(Animalism)<br /> Some masters of Animalsim become so used to cmmunicating with and influencing animals that tehy forget that normally, animals are not as sophisticated as humans. A Cainitie with this derangement treats animals as if they were humans, talking to them like normal people and expecting them to respond as if they were intelligent.<br /> <br /> <b>Unconscious thought reading</b> (Auspex)<br /> A Cainite who is accustomed to using Auspex to read the minds of people in any situation may suddenly find herself unable to shut the mind-reading down. She finds herself overwhelmed with \u201cbackground noise\u201d or, if only in the company of one or two people, answering unasked questions. When this derangement is active, the character suffers a +3 difficulty on all Mental and Social rolls, as wellnas a +1 difficulty to resist frenzy, unless she is in the company of one or two people.\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <b>Disorientation </b>(Celerity)<br /> This derangement afflicts those who rely too heavily on higher levels of Celerity.<br /> The mind becomes accustomed to the slow world that it sees when Celerity is active and becomes disoriented when the world \u201cspeeds up\u201d as the Discipline ends. The character becomes confused<br /> by the pace of the world and suffers a +1 difficulty on all rolls when Celerity is not active. She may insist that the world is moving too fast and that everyone around her should speak slowly and not run.<br /> <br /> <b>Illusion Addiction</b> (Chimestry)<br /> The power of Chimestry is such that it can create anything the wielder immagine... or desire. Sometimes, masters of this Discipline become addicted to the fantasies that Chimestry can create and lose thenmselves in dream worlds of their own making. When this derangement is active, the character sits around for hours creating pleasurable illusions; doing anything else requires the player to succeed in a Wilpowe roll (difficulity 7.)<br /> <br /> <b>Empathic Blindness</b> (Dominate)<br /> This derangement, comparable in many ways to what in modern times is called sociopathy, is found among frequent users of Dominate.<br /> The character becomes blind to the needs, wants and ideas of others. She is incapable of understanding why anyone would not agree with her, follow her commands or do whatever they can to serve her. She suffers a +3 difficulty on Social rolls with those who do not follow her every order and must check for frenzy (difficulty 4) if openly disobeyed.<br /> <br /> <b>Lack of Survival Instinct </b>(Fortitude)<br /> Sometimes, Cainite masters of Fortitude become convinced of their own indestructibility to the point that they disregard even mortal danger. The character is convinced of<br /> her own invincibility in combat. She receives a \u20132 difficulty on all Courage rolls but will not dodge, parry or block an incoming blow and is reluctant to leave combat. If sufficiently wounded, or if friends and allies quit the field, she may decide to withdraw. In order to do so, the player must make a Willpower roll. The difficulty is 9 if friends have quit the battle, 8 if at Wounded or worse with bashing damage, 7 if the damage is lethal and 6 if the damage is aggravated. In cases of mixed damage, use the lowest difficulty.<br /> <br /> <b>Compulsive Invisibility</b> (Obfuscate)<br /> This derangement manifests in users of Obfuscate who either have a touch of paranoia or who insist on walking around cloaked at every possible moment. In the end, the sufferer of this derangement cannot turn off her Obfuscate.<br /> The player roll Willpoer (difficulity 6) to have her character drop the Obfuscate for an important situation, but she will resume invisibility at the earliest opportunity\u200b<br /> <br /> <b>Shadow Infestation</b> (Obtenebration)<br /> This is not a derangement but rather a physical condition that sometimes manifests in users of Obtenebration. The character\u2019s eyes become pools of utter darkness, shadows move of their own accord in her presence, and from time to time, spontaneous Obtenebration effects may manifest. A player can suppress this effect by spending a point of Willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>Disdain of Weakness</b> (Potence)<br /> Masters of Potence can snap wood and crush stone, flesh and bone with ease and must be careful not to damage items and people around them. Those who suffer from this derangement begin to show complete disregard for what they perceive as the weakness of others. The character constantly remarks upon the fragility of items and people around her and always puts all of her strength into any physical action. A handshake crushes the recipient\u2019s hand, a pat on the shoulder becomes a crushing blow, and opening a door likely knocks it off the hinges.\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <b>Unconscious Influence </b>(Presence)<br /> As explained on p.204 of Dark Ages: Vampire, Cainites with Presence sometimes unconsciously activate their powers of charisma. Those who suffer from Unconscious Influence do so constantly, and to make matters worse refuse to believe that this is the case.<br /> When talking to someone whom they would like to influence, they automatically use Entrancement, yet if others accuse them of using Disciplines they will deny it, as they believe that their target finds them utterly charming without any supernatural powers being involved.<br /> <br /> <b>Uncontrolled Shifting</b> (Protean)<br /> Normally, the use of Protean requires conscious effort from the user. Someone suffering from Uncontrolled Shifting, however, finds her body responding to subconcious impulses and her form shifting without her conscious desire.<br /> Should a Gangrel find herself angry, she grows Talons of the Beast; if she fears for her unlife, she assumes Body of Spirit. This not uses up blood, but can also be embarrassing or downright dangerous (activating Talons of the Beast is the Cainite equivalent of drawing a sword).<br /> Spending a point of Wilpower supresses this for a scene, although especially strong stimul might still trigger a change (Storyteller's discretion)<br /> <br /> <b>Blood Fetishism </b>(Quietus)<br /> Most often seen the Warrior Caste of Assamites, this Derangement is an ulthealthy fascination with blood.<br /> Those suffering from it will ofen cut themselves and others to watch the blood flow, feed often and slowly to savor the taste, smear blood on themselves and preform other disturbing acts, from which they gain deep, psychological fulfullment.<br /> <br /> <b>Disregard of Human Form</b> (Serpentis)<br /> With Serpentis, a Follower of Set may approach the perfection of Set. As such, some Setites develop a complete disregard for their human form, instead preferring to adopt one of the forms Serpentis can bestows.<br /> If anyone tries to talk a character out of assuming or remaining in such a form, the player must check for frenzy (difficulity 4), as the suggestion that she should abandon her closeness to the god is insulting\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <b>Uncontrolled Flow </b>(Vicissitude)<br /> Believed by some Tzimisce not to be a derangement but rather an inspired state of mind, this condition affects the character\u2019s control over her fleshcrafting powers.<br /> Spontaneous flesh- and bonecrafting effects manifest from time to time, usually as a response to outside stimuli. An angered Tzimisce might find herself growing claws, while one caressing a favored servant might find herself altering said servant to be more beautiful.\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> So... <br /> ...what do you think about this optional addition?<br /> Used them?<br /> Do you treat the Disciplines as the part of the Curse that eventually consumes the Cainite, and have an inherent danger to embrace the unholy &quot;Gifts of Caine&quot;<br /> Came up with your own ideas to deepen the personal horror that might comes with such powers or never touched the idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T11:38:27-07:00","id":1513216,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't mark them down as derangements on the character sheet, but yes, the psychological impact of disciplines (some as described here) becomes part of characters. Vampirism changes you psychologically on all aspects, including the disciplines. It also makes humans <i>tedious</i> to deal with.<br /> <br /> Your physical form ceases to define your identity when it changes so easily. How you predict and assess the behaviours and emotions of others changes under auspex. Dominate, presence and the physical disciplines (<i>especially</i> celerity) beget impatience. When you can live in a perfect illusion with Chimestry, why live in the miserable drudgery of reality? Dealing with the likes of the Abyss and the Dark Umbra is going to smack your mental health around; your awful clan culture is just the icing on the cake. etc.<br /> <br /> Outside of very specifically themed stories, I don't lean on vampirism as a curse in my games. Vampirism just <i>is, </i>like weather and disease and the food chain. Maybe it's unpleasant, but that's the universe for you. The curse like aspect of the condition is subjective. Hey, it might be, but unless an angel descends with a note from god saying so, the characters have no way of knowing one way or another. I do however play up the fact that you are not and never will again be human, and with every passing night your humanity becomes a faded dream Adapt and put aside your humanity or angst about it for eternity; it's up to the individual.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T13:05:23-07:00","id":1513223,"title":"","content":"As the one who wrote those rules, I give my insight on it here: <a href=\"https://wodarkages.squarespace.com/podcast/players-guide-to-low-clans-part-2\" target=\"_blank\">https://wodarkages.squarespace.com/p...w-clans-part-2</a><br /> (Somewhere around the 45 minute mark, I think, if you don't want to listen to all of it)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T13:13:26-07:00","id":1513224,"title":"","content":"I'd like the notion that some kindred become so skilled with some of their disciplines that they unknowingly use the lower level appilcations all the time. My Malkavian is a prime example of how he doesn't realize that he is using presence to augment his above average charisma in his dealings with humans and his fellow kindred.<br /> <br /> It does add some spice to the struggles of being a kindred and trying to hold onto your humanity and I certainly have no issues that some of them might gain this problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 05-29-2023, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T15:10:20-07:00","id":1513238,"title":"","content":"I have played around with this a few times and I ended up going a slightly different route with it.<br /> <br /> Rather than adding derangements per se, I added permanent vampiric issues.<br /> <br /> So if you start with Auspex then your vampiric senses are always on high and you are given penalties for bright lights and strong smells like garlic. If you have fortitude yes you are more resilient to damage, but your sense of touch is given a penalty. But if you have both Auspex and Fortitude then you keep the bonuses of both, but they cancel each other's negatives.<br /> <br /> This gives the progression of acquiring disciplines more roleplay aspects than a simple power curve increase. Admittedly this can mean that some Clan weaknesses are simulated by discipline interactions rather than core bloodline mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T18:05:01-07:00","id":1513252,"title":"","content":"I think they are very coherent in terms of roleplay, although I have never used them as a mechanic. I mean, I've played Toreador, Nosferatu and Gangrel and I myself have these disturbances, not the character, myself, although in the case of Fortitude it was only with 9mm, but when I could I kept using Auspex and abused Obfuscate in some parts, so this seems to me even palpable to happen. My considerations are more a matter of logic, I can imagine a Tzimice or a Lasombra having their signature disciplines reacting to their emotional state, in the case of the Disregard of Human form, I believe that this would be natural for some, after all what is not lack are kindred who don't see themselves as human so they want to take another form, in fact I think that much is true as the tzimice themselves change form because of a dissatisfaction with their own. In the case of Illusion Addiction, I think it could even yield a good story, like a Ravnos who lost someone important or just misses his old life and therefore fantasizes about it using his discipline, maybe even trying to simulate the taste of food.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-29T18:46:39-07:00","id":1513255,"title":"","content":"I think emotional states may also affect disciplines suddenly coming into effect. A Tzismce finds a mortal quite attractive and feels desire and without knowing makes his or her form more atttractive via a combo of auspex and fleshcrafting. Or my Malkavian is feeling really down and doesn't want to be seen and his advanced knowledge of obsfucate suddenly turns on and he blends into the background. The options are limitless from a storytelling or playing angle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T03:04:51-07:00","id":1513275,"title":"","content":"I find the Celerity one a bit odd. Celerity is so expensive and has such a short duration, that even low generation elders will have it active for more than a few rounds at a time, I don't see how this should result in such an effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T09:18:26-07:00","id":1513297,"title":"","content":"I think in regards to celerity is that maybe kindred find everything moving in such slow motion and they come across as hyperactive and it grates on them. Maybe we can flesh it out more as it's pretty early in the morning and I haven't had my tea yet. Or maybe that would work with an Amalgam perk of Auspex combined with a decent Celerity rating that the Kindred has gotten quite skilled with<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 05-30-2023, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T09:23:12-07:00","id":1513298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513213-discipline-derangements-your-opinion?p=1513238#post1513238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have played around with this a few times and I ended up going a slightly different route with it.<br /> <br /> Rather than adding derangements per se, I added permanent vampiric issues.<br /> <br /> So if you start with Auspex then your vampiric senses are always on high and you are given penalties for bright lights and strong smells like garlic. If you have fortitude yes you are more resilient to damage, but your sense of touch is given a penalty. But if you have both Auspex and Fortitude then you keep the bonuses of both, but they cancel each other's negatives.<br /> <br /> This gives the progression of acquiring disciplines more roleplay aspects than a simple power curve increase. Admittedly this can mean that some Clan weaknesses are simulated by discipline interactions rather than core bloodline mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would handle someone who constantly uses Presence and what would be the drawback?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T10:44:48-07:00","id":1513302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513213-discipline-derangements-your-opinion?p=1513298#post1513298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would handle someone who constantly uses Presence and what would be the drawback?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember correctly I went with Presence being on constantly, to the point it interfered with Stealth attempts. Everyone always notices you, eternally in the spotlight as it were. Needless to say while you can seduce or enthrall someone with ease, trying to go anywhere in public quickly means no feeding or doing anything vampiric. This was then balanced by Obfuscate, which would hide you automatically and you had to struggle to stay visible or noticed. When paired with each other then you could regulate how much attention you got like normal.<br /> <br /> When a Player over uses a Discipline, it is a natural response to try to limit it a bit for game balance. But I find that it often works better for something to work too well and have the PCs deal with the consequences than to say they need to cut back on it.<br /> <br /> There was an old B movie called &quot;<a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0102343/?ref_=nv_sr_srsg_0_tt_7_nm_1_q_love%2520pot\" target=\"_blank\">Love Potion No. 9</a>&quot; which had some researchers create a potion that when diluted and spritzed into the mouth made their voices temporarily enthralling to the opposite gender. Obviously, many dating shenanigans ensue, but at one point in the movie a disliked character gets greedy chugs the undiluted syrup/gel form of the potion and proceeds to speak at a local church.... pretty much the entire town ends up chasing the individual down. Wisely the movie cuts before you get to see the end result of the chase, but the implied results are fairly clear. Yes this approach gets very close to &quot;abusing Charisma or Appearance causes rape&quot; RPG Meme, but it does have some value when dealing with social build characters.<br /> <br /> The interesting thing about Presence is that while its affects are temporary, the reality is that people regularly seek out sensations and feelings to experience them again and again. So even if you use Presence to get past a Bouncer or a Secretary, they might seek you out to feel that again regardless of your interest in them. Additionally, if you are using Presence around lots of people, then I would point out that there aren't any mechanics regarding jealousy in that if you get a group of people who are all infatuated with you, nothing forces them to get along with each other. Imagine a harem anime, except they are all yanderes and have decided to cull the competition. Yes you used Presence to achieve something, but now you have groups of obsessed fans gutting each other and potentially breaking the masquerade.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T12:10:34-07:00","id":1513311,"title":"","content":"A good answer with Presence interfering with your attempts to be subtle and needing advanced knowledge of Obfuscate to balance it out. Love Potion No.9 is a film I haven't thought about in years and to be fair I was more into action films back then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T14:06:17-07:00","id":1513322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513213-discipline-derangements-your-opinion#post1513213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are some examples from those books, but of course, Storytellers and Players are encouraged to come up with their own ideas<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Are there any options or ideas in regard to Thaumaturgy or Necromancy ?<br /> <br /> Certainly these two Disciplines - of the Tremere Vampires ( Warlocks ) and the Giovanni Vampires ( Venetians ) - are clearly and definitely described as particular, difficult complex, and unique to learn and practice. They also have numerous established variations.<br /> <br /> Kindred who extensively practice these Disciplines often choose to focus on Thaumaturgy or Necromancy to a significant, meaningful, and considerable extent.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-30T17:22:27-07:00","id":1513343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513213-discipline-derangements-your-opinion?p=1513322#post1513322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any options or ideas in regard to Thaumaturgy or Necromancy ?</div> </div> </div> </div>The weird thing about magic systems is that they are dependent on the Player being creative as much as they are dependent on the magic mechanics.<br /> <br /> For instance, if a Player had knowledge of chemistry IRL and ran a Tremere with Path of Conjuring..... just end the game now, it will be less painful that way. Likewise, if the Player has hacker experience or computer security knowledge and creates a Tremere with Path of Technomancy, governments will fall and economies will go back to the dark ages, assuming all the nuclear power plants melting down at the same time isn't a greater issue.<br /> <br /> Magic gives you amazing power, the downside is that most people don't consider the ramifications of their choices or actions. There was a computer virus used back in 1982 to try to cause malfunctions in the trans-siberian gas pipeline. It did work, just a little too well. Rather than reducing efficiency and creating supply issues, it doubled the pressure in the pipeline to the point it caused the pipeline to explode. The blast was apparently visible from orbit. Now imagine being able to magically hack every system in the world that isn't magically protected and you are looking at a vampire having a bad hair day and being able to pull a Skynet style Judgement day.<br /> <br /> Perhaps a god complex could be a side issue since you are rewriting reality by your will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T06:42:42-07:00","id":1513386,"title":"","content":"Thaumaturgy doesn't need a Discipline Derangement, every player who gets Thaumaturgy correctly plays the Derangement of becoming obsessed with Thaumaturgy, contantly needing more Paths, more Rituals, trying to solve every problem using Thaumaturgy and fully believing that you can deaign a ritual to handle any situation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T06:56:31-07:00","id":1513387,"title":"","content":"The derangement inherent to necromancy is whatever is wrong with you that caused you to decide to learn necromancy.<br /> Crossover with Wraith: the Oblivion is also likely to cause depression by osmosis.<br /> <br /> I also believe the V20 True Black Hand supplement mentioned that the underworld feels comforting to vampires and that time in the tempest begins to separate their souls into the Psyche/Shadow split, so you could invent necromancer derangements along the lines of preferring to spend time on the other side of the Shroud, shunning life and the living and manifesting signs of a semi-active shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-31T15:43:27-07:00","id":1513467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jackob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513213-discipline-derangements-your-opinion?p=1513386#post1513386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thaumaturgy doesn't need a Discipline Derangement, every player who gets Thaumaturgy correctly plays the Derangement of becoming obsessed with Thaumaturgy, contantly needing more Paths, more Rituals, trying to solve every problem using Thaumaturgy and fully believing that you can deaign a ritual to handle any situation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>And here I thought the discipline derangement was the XP sink for becoming competent in Thaumaturgy requires. When most characters are spending XP to diversify their abilities, you still have not gotten all that good at your initial specialization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-01T11:21:49-07:00","id":1513549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513213-discipline-derangements-your-opinion?p=1513387#post1513387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The derangement inherent to necromancy is whatever is wrong with you that caused you to decide to learn necromancy.<br /> Crossover with Wraith: the Oblivion is also likely to cause depression by osmosis.<br /> <br /> I also believe the V20 True Black Hand supplement mentioned that the underworld feels comforting to vampires and that time in the tempest begins to separate their souls into the Psyche/Shadow split, so you could invent necromancer derangements along the lines of preferring to spend time on the other side of the Shroud, shunning life and the living and manifesting signs of a semi-active shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hecate as they get older and their mastery over necromancy improves, they find being with the dead, ghosts and residing in the realm of the dead then in the world of the living would be a fitting derangement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-02T15:43:30-07:00","id":1513717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jackob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513213-discipline-derangements-your-opinion?p=1513386#post1513386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thaumaturgy doesn't need a Discipline Derangement, every player who gets Thaumaturgy correctly plays the Derangement of becoming obsessed with Thaumaturgy, contantly needing more Paths, more Rituals, trying to solve every problem using Thaumaturgy and fully believing that you can deaign a ritual to handle any situation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>As far as choices, priorities, and activities are considered, creating or altering mzstical, magical, and special objects and items. In addition to this, there is the option of discovering rnew rresources, and travelling to mystic or magical locations and places. A Vampiress can find items and materials needed for spellcasting, rituals, and research.<br /> A Thaumaturgist can also read, copy, modify, create, and write books, notes, scrolls, and literature.<br /> And of course there is the option and the possibility to show and terach Blood Magic to other Vampires - for example to allies and friends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}